<title>SWEDEN: TABLE-Ericsson H1 profit leaps 44 percent.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Ericsson H1 profit leaps 44 percent.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997,</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			    6,095 vs 4,224</p>
<p> Net sales				  72,210 vs 50,030</p>
<p> Order bookings			   87,764 vs 63,345</p>
<p> Shr (crowns)				 4.23 vs 3.06</p>
<p> Mobile Systems sales		   30,100 vs 23,452</p>
<p> Infocom Systems			  21,470 vs 15,945</p>
<p> Mobile Phones and Terminals	  18,387 vs  9,090</p>
<p> Operating costs			  41,957 vs 28,706</p>
<p> Sales, R&amp;D, administration costs   24,093 vs 18,324</p>
<p> Depreciation				1,213 vs  1,034</p>
<p> Operating profit			  6,913 vs  4,233  Minorities</p>
<p>				   702 vs    160</p>
<p>NOTE -- Analysts expected Swedish telecoms group AB LM Ericsson to post a first half pre-tax profit of 5.11 billion crowns. Ericsson said it continued to take market share in mobile telephones and that Infocom division sales were still unsatisfactory.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
